    "summary": "Repaired an instance error and regenerated a passing model.\n\nRoot cause: the girder section in the instance had top slab thickness t_top = 0.20 m, contradicting the description (\"top slab 0.18 m thick\"). The accepted girder.single.A / girder.single.I decisions (1.06052 m², 0.25166 m⁴) had been computed from the correct 0.18 m section, so the L2-1 check (re-computing each member's parameters from its provenance decisions) failed on the geometry mismatch. Correcting the instance to t_top = 0.18 m invalidated the dependent girder decisions (girder.single.A/I, girder.A/I, girder.w, girder.m) and lane.mu; these were re-proposed, the modal analysis re-run, and lane.mu re-derived.\n\nModel (spine_beam_2d, simply supported, 25 m span):\n- Section: precast prestressed small box, C40, 5 girders/span. Single mid-girder A = 1.06052 m², I = 0.25166 m⁴ (integrated from the corrected section); combined A = 5.30260 m², I = 1.25829 m⁴. Ec = 32500 MPa, γ = 26 kN/m³, w = 137.87 kN/m, m = 14.054 t/m (self-weight of girders only).\n- Supports: two abutments, each with 10 plain laminated elastomeric bearings (2 per girder end, 300×350 mm, 4 layers × 8 mm, G from code default). S = 10.096, Kv = 14163.2 MN/m, Kh = 32.81 MN/m per line; vertical/longitudinal springs, free rotation.\n- Live load: Highway Class II, one-way, 4 design lanes, ξ = 0.67, qk = 7.875 kN/m², Pk = 232.5 kN, μ = 0.2409 (from f1 = 4.272 Hz per JTG D60-2015 4.3.2).\n\nResults: f1 = 4.272 Hz; girder self-weight reactions 1723.3 kN per support and midspan moment 10770.9 kN·m; lane-load max positive moment 6878.4 kN·m at midspan; no negative lane moment."
